&lt;h1&gt;📘 Topic: Cable Locks and Physical Deterrents&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain:&lt;/strong&gt; D4 – Physical and Environmental Security&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; #cissp #physicalsecurity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🧾 Definition&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-definition&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-definition&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cable locks are physical deterrents used to secure portable devices (laptops, monitors) by mechanically attaching them to an immovable object; they are one element of physical security and asset protection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔑 Key Points&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-points&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-points&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cable locks deter opportunistic theft but are not foolproof against determined attackers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combine cable locks with asset tracking, access control, and CCTV for stronger protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For data centers, stronger physical controls such as locked racks and controlled access are appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚠️ CISSP Insight&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-cissp-insight&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-cissp-insight&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSP teaches layered physical controls: deterrence, detection, delay, and response. Cable locks are a low-cost deterrent but should be part of a broader physical security program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚔️ Key Difference / Trap&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-difference--trap&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-difference--trap&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deterrent vs Preventive control&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cable locks deter casual theft but do not prevent all removal methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trap:&lt;/strong&gt; Relying solely on cable locks without access control or inventory reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🏗️ Example&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-example&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-example&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Workplace laptops are secured with cable locks in public areas, asset tags are logged, and security checks verify presence at the end of the day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;📚 References&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-references&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-references&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Annex A (Physical security)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NIST SP 800-161 (Supply chain and physical security considerations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔁 Quick Recall&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-quick-recall&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-quick-recall&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cable locks = cheap deterrent; use alongside access control and asset management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>[03] CISSP Cheatsheet - Layer 3 Networking (Routing &amp; Segmentation)</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/04_playbooks/cissp/d6/25-layer-3/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/04_playbooks/cissp/d6/25-layer-3/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #6b7280; display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px;&#34;&gt;
  
    &lt;span style=&#34;display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;&#34;&gt;
      By:
      
        
        
        
        
          
          
          
          
          &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/authors/your-name/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34; style=&#34;display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-weight: 600; color: #0a66c2; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;&#34; onmouseover=&#34;this.style.borderBottom=&#39;1px solid #0a66c2&#39;&#34; onmouseout=&#34;this.style.borderBottom=&#39;1px solid transparent&#39;&#34;&gt;
